---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About · ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Who Pip is, and why tiny frogs keep appearing in public places."
			image="/frog-scene-found.svg"
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<article class="about">
				<img class="about-frog" src="/frog-pip.svg" alt="Pip the frog figurine" width="200" height="175" />
				<h1>about pip</h1>
				<p>
					Pip is a cute little 3D-printed frog figurine. Copies of Pip get left in parks, on ledges,
					near library shelves, and other quiet public places — small surprises for whoever notices.
				</p>
				<p>
					This website is the easter egg that comes with them. Nothing to buy, nothing to join. Just
					a soft place on the internet where Pip keeps a short journal of sitting still and watching
					the world hop by.
				</p>
				<p>
					If you found a Pip: you can leave it for someone else, take a photo, or simply say hello
					here. Pip does not mind either way.
				</p>
				<p class="quiet">
					<a href="/blog">Read the journal →</a>
				</p>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.about {
		max-width: 36rem;
	}
	.about-frog {
		width: 140px;
		height: auto;
		display: block;
		margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
		animation: softbob 3.2s ease-in-out infinite;
	}
	.quiet {
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}
	@keyframes softbob {
		0%,
		100% {
			transform: translateY(0);
		}
		50% {
			transform: translateY(-6px);
		}
	}
</style>
